# pr-hero's own exclusions, on top of the 9 shipped defaults (lockfiles, minified, snapshots).
# Dialect: a gitignore(5) subset, read from the BASE ref under CI. Last matching rule wins.
#
# Scope: PROSE FILES ONLY, and only at the top level of three directories. Research notes, benchmark
# ledgers and the roadmap are argued in review comments and PR descriptions, not by a hunter, and
# their diffs are large — reviewing them spends budget on text that cannot break at runtime.
#
# The rules are `*.md`, never `**`, so anything else that lands in those directories — a script, a
# case list, a config, a fixture — stays in scope by construction rather than by a negation someone
# has to remember to add. Our own corpus is the reason two goldens live in material a blanket
# `docs/**` or `*.md` rule would hide: shell under `set -u` inside a markdown runbook, and a
# macOS-only `sed -i ''` in a shell script. Both are Martian Cal.com goldens; the attribution that
# records that class is docs/research/local-logic-misses.md. Runbooks, workflows, prompts, README
# and CLAUDE.md stay in scope everywhere.
#
# Known and accepted: a markdown file under these three directories is unreviewed even when it quotes
# a command. docs/research/scout-design.md is the live example. Prose meant to be EXECUTED belongs
# in docs/release-runbook.md or in a script, both of which are reviewed.

docs/research/*.md
docs/benchmarks/*.md
docs/history/*.md
ROADMAP.md
